# CP16 — final tidy. The last code commit before submission.
#
# F33  .gitignore audited against every path in `git ls-files out/`.
# F34  python-multipart pinned; /voice/extract takes an UploadFile.
# F35  The transcription findings moved into README results.
# F36  next_month's demo-path-only scope, and clip 2's variance, recorded.
# F37  Every README number re-verified against its artefact by hand.

.gitignore
requirements.txt
settle/api/voice.py
KNOWN_LIMITATIONS.md
README.md
SPEC.md
PLAN.md
checkpoints/cp16.allowlist

# --- Why the audit rather than a fourth one-line fix -------------------------
#
# `git check-ignore` short-circuits on tracked files and reports nothing, so the
# obvious check says every committed artefact is fine. `--no-index` asks the
# question properly: would this path be ignored if it were untracked? Two were —
# out/razorpay_demo.json and out/voice_demo.json — tracked only because they had
# been force-added at a checkpoint whose allowlist excluded .gitignore.
#
# That is now nine committed artefacts and nine negations, verified in both
# directions: every tracked path is committable, and every run artefact
# (llm_cache, batch, audit_*, sensitivity, model pickles, razorpay_raw,
# razorpay_demo_state) is still ignored.

# --- The raw-body path on /voice/extract is kept, not replaced ---------------
#
# F34 asked for UploadFile and that is what the route takes. It also still reads
# a raw body when the content type is not multipart, because `viewer/index.html`
# posts that way and the viewer is not on this allowlist.
#
# Keeping it is the better shape regardless. Breaking the endpoint's only caller
# in order to adopt a tidier signature would be a refactor charged to the demo,
# two days before submission, for no behaviour a judge sees. Both paths are
# exercised: multipart returns 200 with the full trace, raw body returns the
# same trace, and the error paths (400 empty, 415 wrong suffix) are unchanged.

# --- F37: one gap found, in the direction that matters least ------------------
#
# 46 curated figures checked by hand against out/metrics.json,
# out/model_report.json, out/razorpay_demo.json and out/voice_demo.json, then a
# full token sweep of the prose against every artefact plus PRIORS and SPEC.
#
# Nothing in the README was unbacked. The single discrepancy ran the other way:
# `pay_TWrJELO1R1PGeA`, the declined payment, was in the artefact and not in the
# README, so the sentence claiming "a real decline beside a real capture" named
# only the capture. The id is in the table now, and the claim is checkable.
